{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Scope extended: the canonical guidance is the root cause, and it was out of scope\n\nRe-measured this bug's central claim on current `origin/main` (`73e90b296e2`) and then went looking for *why* authors keep writing the clause. The answer is a document this ticket did not cover.\n\n**Re-measurement confirms and strengthens the original finding.** `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` prints `active=648 new=28 increased=0 stale=0` and exits 0 — up one from the `new=27` recorded here in 2026-09. More importantly, the counter is nonzero **by design**, not by accident:\n\n- `new` counts every mechanism in the tree but absent from the baseline, admitted or not.\n- The baseline has no write path for new keys. Its only mutator is `drain_stale` (`scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:102`), which returns `{key: 1 for key in baseline if key in current}` under the docstring \"Keep active baseline keys without adding new current keys\".\n- The CLI exposes only `(--check | --update-stale)`, mutually exclusive. There is no `--lock`.\n\nSo `new=0` is reachable **only** by deleting all 28 admitted mechanisms from the tree — 22 `ci_gate` steps, 3 shared `test_helper` modules (`tests/_child_hooks.py`, `_crash_guard.py`, `_sandbox_capabilities.py`), `RefLockPushError`, `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT`, `compact.snapshot_alpha` — each deliberate work admitted with a reasoned marker citing its own ticket. Permanent `new>0` is the ratchet's steady state: it never blesses growth into the baseline, it admits growth through in-tree markers, and that asymmetry is what makes it a ratchet rather than a freeze.\n\n**The root cause is `AGENTS.md:381`.** It describes this gate as one that \"**fails on any `new>0`**\". The script's own contract (`check_mechanism_delta.py:26-29`) says it \"exits zero only when every new/increased key has a non-blank marker and no marker is blank\". The gate is authoritative, so the canonical guidance is wrong — and unlike the plan guide, which is read on demand, `AGENTS.md` is loaded into every harness at launch. An author who trusts it writes `new=0` and cannot discover the error until close.\n\nThat makes this ticket's AC1-AC3 a partial fix: they would have corrected `writing-a-passing-plan.md` while leaving the more authoritative document still teaching the misread.\n\n**Fourth instance, caught pre-review today.** `361f-0a5c-bd12-463b` AC3 carried the identical clause. It was amended to assert exit 0 before its plan review ran, so this one cost no close-time investigation — but it is the fourth ticket to inherit the clause after `f5f5` AC5, `b939` AC2, and the `db2c`/`25a4` pair.\n\n**Added AC4** covering the `AGENTS.md` paragraph, with a binary check, plus an instruction to verify the adjacent complexity-ratchet sentence against `check_complexity_baseline.py` in the same pass and correct it only if it misstates that gate's contract. Description also records the fresh measurement and the no-write-path evidence."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793472522098495001,"uuid":"9a60f8c3-96c5-4ff4-b8e7-3232351d34e8"}